{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473762-question-regarding-acquiring-new-gifts-in-werewolf-20th-a","id":1473762,"title":"Question regarding acquiring new Gifts in Werewolf 20th A","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-01T11:30:01-08:00","id":1473762,"title":"Question regarding acquiring new Gifts in Werewolf 20th A","content":"I'm curious to know if anyone has an alternative method for their players to acquire new Gifts rather than summoning a spirit to teach it to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T11:51:32-08:00","id":1473764,"title":"","content":"You can learn gifts from another garou, but that process takes much longer than learning from spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T13:51:39-08:00","id":1473772,"title":"","content":"Is there are particular reason to need another method? Though you don't need to summon one, you need to find one. Summoning is just very useful because you can get the exact type you want. But almost every Sept is going to have ancestor spirits around (pretty common for Gifts), and spirits associated with the Caern Totem, the pack Totems of the NPCs, and spirits naturally drawn to the nature of the Caern. Lots of spirits are not hard to predict areas where you can find them.<br /> <br /> That said pack Totems sometimes grant Gifts as part of their perks, and powerful spirits can straight up reward Gifts if it suits them rather than the Garou needing to actually seek them out. Doing something important enough to get on the good side of an Incarna could easily result in one of said Incarna's avatars finding you and offering to teach the Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T06:02:25-08:00","id":1473820,"title":"","content":"There was a rule of thumb that a caern of level X would house spirits in its vicinity that teach up to level X. Not sure if the rule made it into W20.<br /> <br /> Previous editions mentioned that learning a Gift from another garou (or fera, I guess), requires trail and error to some extend, which can be painful to dangerous, if you think about Silver Claws.<br /> <br /> More speculative ideas would be:<ul><li>Trying to learn a Gift from a spirit inside a fetish. Communication with spirits inside a fetish might be possible through meditation. It is part of the process attuning to a fetish but not necessarily limited to this use....</li> <li>It might be a stretch, but Ancestors Background mentions: While it is more difficult to contact a specific ancestor, successful contact provides either useful advice or precognitive visions at the discretion of the Storyteller.&quot; Here you could see knowledge of a Gift as useful advice.... possibly. Mokol\u00e9 use Mnesis to learn Gifts, so.....</li> <li>Kinfolk, too, might teach a Gift if you find a Kinfolk possessing knowledge of a Gift.</li> </ul><br /> Before W20 there was, I think in the sourcebook Axis Mundi, the idea to ignore subplots about Gift learning and just grant them, as a boon from Pack Totem or tribal Totem or whatever. While clearly an alternative to the usual Setting, it makes things easier for ST and Players, if they can focus on the main story and not be bothered to roleplay Gift learning. Also, moving it to the Downtime is also acceptable, I guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T12:43:50-08:00","id":1473849,"title":"","content":"The Caern level = Gift Rank you can learn is still in W20, but it's an in-universe tradition rather than a mechanical rule. Of course tradition is very important to both Garou and spirits, so ignoring that is meant to increase the narrative steps of getting the spirit to agree in the first place.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you're at a Sept with a Caern equal to or greater in rank than the level of Gift you want to get, it's intended to be handwaved beyond having the Sept's permission in the first place. This also help create one of the reasons Septs in a given area try to have good relations: to facilitate the trade of access to high level Caern spirits for chiminage from the Septs with weaker Caerns.<br /> <br /> If you don't have access to an appropriate Caern, it's not supposed to stop you from getting Gifts, it just means you've got to do more to get them. Summoning, significant chiminage offerings, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T14:17:53-08:00","id":1473862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473762-question-regarding-acquiring-new-gifts-in-werewolf-20th-a?p=1473849#post1473849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caern level = Gift Rank you can learn is still in W20, but it's an in-universe tradition rather than a mechanical rule. Of course tradition is very important to both Garou and spirits, so ignoring that is meant to increase the narrative steps of getting the spirit to agree in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Gifts have ties to rank, I don't think that garou should in-universe judge a Caerns strength on a 1 to 5 scale....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473762-question-regarding-acquiring-new-gifts-in-werewolf-20th-a?p=1473849#post1473849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, if you're at a Sept with a Caern equal to or greater in rank than the level of Gift you want to get, it's intended to be handwaved beyond having the Sept's permission in the first place. This also help create one of the reasons Septs in a given area try to have good relations: to facilitate the trade of access to high level Caern spirits for chiminage from the Septs with weaker Caerns.<br /> <br /> If you don't have access to an appropriate Caern, it's not supposed to stop you from getting Gifts, it just means you've got to do more to get them. Summoning, significant chiminage offerings, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember reading about this, but it is an interesting aspect for relations between septs in a given area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T14:34:15-08:00","id":1473863,"title":"","content":"Caerns are supposed to have a higher number of spirits than normal because it's a caern, and the spirits are seeking the benefits of being near a caern totem, the stronger spiritual energy there, and having lots of Garou around. So it'd be easy for an ST to have certain spirits around who don't need to be summoned. And they even be intelligent or friendly enough they can speak the Garou Tongue, and a Garou doesn't even need to use Spirit Speech to communicate.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is that the pack totems can intercede on their pack members behalf. They probably have experience with a certain number of spirits, especially those that belong to the same brood as them. So an ST can make some spirits additionally known to them. Plus the pack totem itself might be able to teach certain Gifts if it makes sense for the kind of spirit it is.<br /> <br /> These still involve spirits teaching the Garou, but they don't necessarily need to be summoned.<br /> <br /> If you want to avoid spirits in general, it's more limited. The other method is for a Garou, who already knows the Gift, to teach it to them, but this is something that general angers the spirits.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any alternate methods off hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}